# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what ships in the .vsix.
# An allowlist (instead of a denylist) because vsce does not read .gitignore, and
# untracked local files (CLAUDE.md, .claude/) would otherwise leak into a public package.
# vsce always includes package.json and the README. Never combine with `files` in
# package.json: vsce aborts when both exist.
# CI checks the result with scripts/check-vsix.mjs: any new file that must ship needs its `!`
# line here AND, if it is essential, an entry in that script's required list.
# Ships: the two bundles, the two media files the manifest points at, LICENSE and CHANGELOG, and the
# language catalogs (package.nls*.json and l10n/): vsce adds only package.json and the README by
# itself, so without these lines the extension would ship in English only (E11-i18n).
# media/icon.svg is the SOURCE of media/icon.png and stays out; README images live in
# docs/images/ (not packaged: vsce rewrites their relative links to GitHub raw URLs).
# Regenerate the icon (resvg-js-cli, version pinned, not a devDependency; 256 px wide):
#   npx -y @resvg/resvg-js-cli@2.6.2-beta.1 --fit-width 256 media/icon.svg media/icon.png
**
!dist/extension.js
!dist/modWorker.js
!dist/webview/**
!package.nls.json
!package.nls.*.json
!l10n/**
!media/activity.svg
!media/chat-tab-light.svg
!media/chat-tab-dark.svg
!media/icon.png
!LICENSE*
!CHANGELOG.md
